The '''1967 NFL/AFL draft''' was conducted March 14–15, 1967, at the [[Gotham Hotel]] in [[New York City]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.footballgeography.com/nfl-draft-sites/ |title=NFL Draft Locations |date=October 2, 2014 |website=www.footballgeography.com |access-date=October 23, 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150905090250/http://www.footballgeography.com/nfl-draft-sites/ |archive-date=September 5, 2015 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Salomone|first1=Dan|title=NFL Draft headed to Chicago in 2015|url=http://www.giants.com/news-and-blogs/article-1/NFL-Draft-headed-to-Chicago-in-2015/3ac322b1-3b4c-4a16-aba7-6e08d31b1756|access-date=June 3, 2015|publisher=[[New York Giants]]|work=Giants.com|date=October 2, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150930065327/http://www.giants.com/news-and-blogs/article-1/NFL-Draft-headed-to-Chicago-in-2015/3ac322b1-3b4c-4a16-aba7-6e08d31b1756|archive-date=September 30, 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name=cpfr>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=4GAqAAAAIBAJ&sjid=1U4EAAAAIBAJ&pg=7180%2C2711601 |newspaper=Milwaukee Sentinel |agency=Associated Press |title=Colts pick 1st in grid draft today |date=March 14, 1967 |page=2, part 2 }}</ref> It was the first [[common draft]] between the [[National Football League]] (NFL) and the [[American Football League]] (AFL), part of the [[AFL–NFL merger]] agreement of June 1966.

This draft was delayed as new guidelines were established; [[Redshirt (college sports)|redshirt]] (or "future") players were no longer eligible.<ref name=pgdbt>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=06dVAAAAIBAJ&sjid=-uADAAAAIBAJ&pg=2739%2C2556011 |newspaper=Eugene Register-Guard |location=Oregon |agency=UPI |title=Pro grid draft begins Tuesday |date=March 13, 1967 |page=2B }}</ref> It began on a Tuesday in mid-March (first five rounds); the previous two years the leagues held their separate drafts on the final Saturday of November, immediately following the college football regular season.

The [[1967 NFL expansion draft|expansion]] [[1967 New Orleans Saints season|New Orleans Saints]] initially had the [[List of first overall National Football League Draft picks|first overall pick]]; a&nbsp;week before the draft, they traded it to the [[1967 Baltimore Colts season|Baltimore Colts]],<ref name=bccuozz>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=zadVAAAAIBAJ&sjid=-uADAAAAIBAJ&pg=7017%2C1249187 |work=Eugene Register-Guard |location=Oregon |agency=Associated Press |title=Baltimore Colts deal Cuozzo to Saints |date=March 7, 1967 |page=2B}}</ref> who selected defensive end [[Bubba Smith]] of [[1966 Michigan State Spartans football team|Michigan&nbsp;State]].<ref name=cpsm>{{cite news |url=https://news.google.com/newspapers?id=1KdVAAAAIBAJ&sjid=-uADAAAAIBAJ&pg=6828%2C2702871 |work=Eugene Register-Guard |location=Oregon |agency=Associated Press |title=Colts pick Smith as No. 1 draft choice |date=March 14, 1967 |page=2B}}</ref>

